executor-benchmark: time-based mode, block count and execution latency reporting

* BENCHMARK_DURATION_SECS: stop generating blocks after the given time
  (time-based runs); unset keeps the block-count behaviour.
* "Overall" results also report the elapsed time (HH:MM:SS), the number of
  generated blocks and blocks/s (log lines and JSON).
* aptos-block-executor records the execution time of transaction incarnations;
  executor-benchmark prints their p10..p99.999 ("<prefix> pXX: N us").
* create-db accepts an existing data directory (P-Directories are bind-mounted
  onto its subdirectories before the run).

Base: aptos-labs/aptos-core main at commit
      2f99b2fbeb63ee3ee4d8fbdbd1aba164e39ed7b8 (2025-12-29)
Apply: git apply 0001-executor-benchmark-time-based-mode-and-measurements.patch
License: this patch modifies aptos-core and is subject to aptos-core's
         Innovation-Enabling Source Code License (see LICENSE and README.md).

